{"title":"CEMC Senior Competition","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>Canadian Senior Mathematics Competition</b>, or the CSMC, is a contest administered by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Centre_for_Education_in_Mathematics_and_Computing\" title=\"Centre for Education in Mathematics and Computing\">Centre for Education in Mathematics and Computing</a>. It is for students in Grade 12 or lower. It is highly recommended you take this test if you wish to apply to the University of Waterloo. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CEMC_Senior_Competition&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CSMC_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"CSMC Problems and Solutions\">CSMC Problems and Solutions</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=CEMC_Senior_Competition&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017131057\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.007 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.011 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 10/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 310/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.975      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.975      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:25735:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 202